{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_control_probe_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"newraft_doc\\\",\\\"follower_abort\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Isolated control for the committed-log-replay finding: bootstrap a single voter, become leader, commit five commands, never snapshot (SnapshotThreshold huge, SnapshotInterval 10m), shut down and restart on the same InmemCommitTrackingStore/InmemStore/InmemSnapshotStore with RestoreCommittedLogs left at its default false. Emits only the control setup event and the control result event, so the control is scored independently of the failing mode.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"RestoreCommittedLogs defaults to false (config.go), so this is the ordinary restart path with identical durable state and identical missing snapshot.\\\",\\\"The stores and the bootstrap/commit sequence are the same as in the failing probe, so the only difference is the replay of committed logs at startup.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No multi-voter cluster, no configuration change, no partitions.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"protocol_version\\\":3,\\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"election_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"trailing_logs\\\":10}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Real bootstrap, real election, real applies, real shutdown and restart on the same durable stores with a fresh transport; no fabricated log entries or configuration state.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_control_restart\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"control_start\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshot_count\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0}]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[{\\\"event\\\":\\\"control_restart\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"restore_committed\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_control_restart\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"servers_after\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control expectation: without replaying committed logs, the restarted node keeps its bootstrapped configuration, isolating the replay as the cause of the loss observed with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled.\\\"}]\n}\ni=d['interpretations'][0]\ni['experiment_id']='8efd0d1e3da9484e926cab983024d9c3-experiment'\ni['conclusion']='violated'\ni['defect_claim']='asserted'\ni['executions']={'430d7ba602ed4666bdfe63a96c71e2fc':[1],'d2d1cb0951b74a2984ec525710e4c740':[1,3]}\ni['joint_history']=\\\"Both receipts belong to the same question and harness family (single-voter restart probe, then two-voter snapshot/configuration-change probe) executed from the same snapshot; the second probe was built after the first receipt confirmed the empty-configuration case, to test whether a snapshot-carried configuration makes the loss stale rather than empty, and whether that stale base changes a later decision.\\\"\ni['answers']={\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-gap-0\\\":{\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Resolved by the retained receipt d2d1cb0951b74a2984ec525710e4c740: after a snapshot that carries configuration {A,B}@1, a committed AddVoter C at index 8 and four further commits (staged commit 11), the restarted node reports servers_after=2 while its continuously running peer reports 3 and its own log still contains the newest configuration entry at index 8 (comparison 0 violated, witness index 1). That stale base then changes a real decision: a later AddVoter E against the restarted node returned no error and the cluster converged on 3 members with contains_c_final=false on both nodes (comparison 2 violated, witness index 3), i.e. voter C was silently removed although no request removed it. The control run in the same receipt with RestoreCommittedLogs=false kept 3 members and ended with 4 members including C (observed at parsed index 5, whose comparison the controller recorded as unknown because both modes emit the same result event name).\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":True}}\ni['counterevidence']=[\n \\\"The control mode inside the same receipt (parsed index 5) kept servers_after=3 and the later change produced 4 members including C, so the stale base is specific to the replayed committed prefix rather than to snapshots or configuration changes in general.\\\",\n \\\"The restarted node still held every committed entry on disk (log_last_index=12), so this is lost configuration context, not lost data; the entry would be re-read only from a snapshot install.\\\"]\ni['limitations']=[\n \\\"The control mod in the same receipt was scored 'unknown' by the controller because both modes emit the same result event name; its observed values at index 5 are cited as observations, and the dedicated control experiment requested in this update is meant to produce an independently scored control.\\\",\n \\\"Voter C never runs in this probe, so the probe does not show whether C itself would notice the removal; the finding is about the configuration each running node decides with.\\\",\n \\\"Executed scope is two in-memory voters at protocol version 3 with 50ms timeouts and one committed single-server change; joint consensus and multi-step changes are not exercised.\\\"]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -5\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
