{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Retained receipt d2d1cb0951b74a2984ec525710e4c740 confirmed the gap I registered: after a snapshot carrying {A,B} and a committed AddVoter C at index 8 (staged commit 11), the restarted node adopted the stale configuration (servers_after=2 while its peer reports 3; comparison 0 violated, witness index 1) and then a later AddVoter E returned no error while both nodes converged without C (comparison 2 violated, witness index 3) — a legitimately added voter silently dropped. The interpretation now records both receipts (empty-configuration case plus stale-configuration decision consequence) as violated/asserted with joint history, and the gap is marked resolved; the control mode's observed values are cited even though the controller scored that comparison unknown because both modes share a result event name. Submitted an isolated control experiment whose only result event is the non-replay restart, so a clean control verdict is possible.\"}"}}
